Replace line 381 with the constructed alias using an effectively-final loop variable:
```java
for (int i = 0; i < 20; i++) {
    final String alias = "idp-alias-" + i;   // effectively final for method reference
    IdentityProviderRepresentation idpRep = new IdentityProviderRepresentation();
    idpRep.setAlias(alias);
    idpRep.setEnabled((i % 2) == 0);
    idpRep.setDisplayName("Broker " + i);
    idpRep.setProviderId("keycloak-oidc");
    if (i >= 10) idpRep.getConfig().put(OrganizationModel.BROKER_PUBLIC, Boolean.TRUE.toString());
    testRealm().identityProviders().create(idpRep).close();
    getCleanup().addCleanup(testRealm().identityProviders().get(alias)::remove);  // use variable, not literal
}
```
Apply the same fix at lines 303 and 425. Alternatively, replace with the idiomatic `getCleanup().addIdentityProviderAlias(alias)` which uses the dedicated per-alias cleanup path in `TestCleanup.executeCleanup` (lines 142-151) that already tolerates `NotFoundException`.

